      "math_academy_id": "e-12628",
      "problem": "In a regular polygon, all the exterior angles have a measure of $20^\\circ.$ How many sides does the polygon have?",
      "worked_solution": "The sum of the exterior angles of any polygon is $360^\\circ.$ \n\nFor a regular polygon, all exterior angles have the same measure. \n\nTherefore, the number of exterior angles is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{360^\\circ}{20^\\circ} = 18\\,.\n$$\n\nThe number of sides, then, is also $18.$",
